00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.740
Yeah, keep going, keep going.

00:00:28.151 --> 00:00:30.351
(Kristen screams)

00:00:30.351 --> 00:00:33.101
(dramatic music)

00:00:37.976 --> 00:00:39.763
(audience cheers)

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:43.213
- Wow. Please welcome Chef
Kristen Kish, everybody.

00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:44.347
(audience cheering)
Meet Joshua.

00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:47.224
- Hi.
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:47.224 --> 00:00:48.057
- Meet Christine.
- Very well.

00:00:48.057 --> 00:00:48.920
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.790
- So would y'all ever
climb down a waterfall?

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.623
I would.

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:52.530
- Yes, I have.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.401
- [Kelly] You have?

00:00:53.401 --> 00:00:54.234
- I have, yeah.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.530
- Wait, I, I learned a fun fact.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.660
You also had a show on National
Geographic, is that correct?

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.235
- I did a special on National Geographic.

00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:00.068
- [Kristen] Okay.

00:01:00.068 --> 00:01:00.901
- But it was all under the water.

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:01.734
- [Kristen] Got it.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:02.970
So I am now taking your
place above, and then

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:03.803
we can come together.
- Well,

00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:04.636
I'll trade with you.

00:01:04.636 --> 00:01:05.610
That looked really nice to me.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:06.443
- [Kristen] Yeah.

00:01:06.443 --> 00:01:07.276
- Underwater is cool too.

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:08.109
- Underwater was very cool, yeah.

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:09.980
- Would you ever climb down a waterfall?

00:01:10.952 --> 00:01:11.785
- No.

00:01:11.785 --> 00:01:12.618
(all laugh)

00:01:12.618 --> 00:01:14.100
I wanted to lie, and I was like,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.570
I'm not going to do that.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.010
I'll swim at the bottom.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.300
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And like, wave to y'all.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.400
- I would totally climb,
I just think it'd be fun.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.260
Okay, tell us about your
new show, it looks awesome.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.270
- So, I mean, the title
would imply restaurants

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.140
at the end of the world.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.870
- And I am a chef, so we're
gathering those things

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.430
and bringing them together.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.560
But the thing that I
love most about this show

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.560
is being able to live
how someone else's live.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.393
How, how they live.

00:01:35.393 --> 00:01:37.560
Because, I was adopted
when I was four months old.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.971
I was raised in Michigan,
and the idea, and like this,

00:01:39.971 --> 00:01:40.980
- [Audience Member] Woo!

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:41.813
- Yay!

00:01:41.813 --> 00:01:43.008
- Michigan, give it up for Michigan.

00:01:43.008 --> 00:01:45.960
(everyone applauds)

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.030
- This idea of, the
fact that I was chosen,

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.550
and that I could have landed up anywhere,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.130
living with any family,
anywhere across the world.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.670
And this idea always fueled
the curiosity for my travel.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.960
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So it's,

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.700
it is an exercise in human empathy.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.300
It's an exercise in education
in food, location, culture,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.280
and just walking the path

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.320
that someone else walks every single day

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.377
and trying to learn as
much as you can about it.

00:02:09.377 --> 00:02:11.490
(audience cheering)
- (indistinct) That's amazing.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.600
So what are we doing today?

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.468
- [Kristen] All right, so.

00:02:13.468 --> 00:02:14.301
- It looks like a game.

00:02:14.301 --> 00:02:15.780
- Yeah it is a game, I've heard,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.160
and I've watched several,
- What?

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.570
- several clips that you love a game,

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:19.935
and you are very competitive.
- What?

00:02:19.935 --> 00:02:21.750
So I figured I'd give you all a little bit

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.695
of a taste of some ingredients.

00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:24.528
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:24.528 --> 00:02:27.210
- Of some things and dishes
from these four places,

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.130
Brazil, Norway, Maine, and Panama.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:29.963
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:31.950
- And a little game that
I, slash your producers,

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.975
have named Traveling Taste Test.

00:02:33.975 --> 00:02:37.600
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.640
- Okay, so how do we play?

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.473
How do we play?

00:02:39.473 --> 00:02:40.860
- All right, so the rules are very simple.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.231
- Okay.
- You have 30 seconds.

00:02:42.231 --> 00:02:43.064
- Okay.

00:02:43.064 --> 00:02:46.140
- 30 seconds to un-cloche these items.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.060
Under each cloche is a dish.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.546
Now, each dish contains an ingredient

00:02:49.546 --> 00:02:50.610
(whooshing sound effects)

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.920
from one of these four places.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.650
So, you have 30 seconds
to try all the dishes

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.220
and correctly place a location
card in front of each plate

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.950
that you think that dish is representing.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.719
- Okay, and once again,
you called this a what?

00:03:03.719 --> 00:03:04.793
- A cloche.
(Joshua laughing)

00:03:04.793 --> 00:03:06.468
- Sure, totally.
- Yes, yeah.

00:03:06.468 --> 00:03:07.590
- [Kelly] I was like, what?

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.423
- [Kristen] A cover.

00:03:08.423 --> 00:03:10.512
- A cloche, I shall use
this to sound fancy.

00:03:10.512 --> 00:03:12.090
- [Joshua] (indistinct) when you.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.262
- Yeah, cloche, you can un-cloche that.

00:03:13.262 --> 00:03:16.170
- We're going to un-cloche
in front of the audience.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.003
- I like it.

00:03:17.003 --> 00:03:17.836
- Okay, undress all your plates.

00:03:17.836 --> 00:03:18.768
- Hey, the more you know, I like learning.

00:03:18.768 --> 00:03:19.751
(audience laughs)
- So.

00:03:19.751 --> 00:03:23.310
All right, so competitions are no fun

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.635
unless someone wins something
and two people lose.

00:03:24.635 --> 00:03:25.710
- Oh, yeah.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.930
- So two of you will lose, by the way.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.116
- I'm sorry.
- I'm so sorry.

00:03:29.116 --> 00:03:31.140
- I'm so sorry for your loss.
- And each,

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.220
each one of you is gonna play

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.180
for a section of the audience.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.844
So, Kelly, we're gonna
give you this section here.

00:03:34.844 --> 00:03:36.550
(audience cheering)
- What's up, what's up?

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.385
- Joshua you got the middle,

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.218
and Christine, you got the-

00:03:40.218 --> 00:03:41.051
- [Christine] I got the (indistinct).

00:03:41.051 --> 00:03:41.890
(audience cheering)

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:46.230
All right, so there is a huge
prize, it's a huge prize.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.063
- Okay.

00:03:47.063 --> 00:03:48.960
- And I'm gonna say something
absolutely ridiculous

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.830
and it's like silly, but
it's a, it is a pun, so.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.663
- I love it.

00:03:53.663 --> 00:03:54.756
- Please play like ninjas.

00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:55.589
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:55.589 --> 00:03:56.422
Shall we?

00:03:56.422 --> 00:03:57.870
Hint, hint, there's a great cooking brand.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.920
- I got it, I got it.
- It's a ninja prize.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.910
- I got it.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.890
- So, 30 seconds on the clock.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:02.910
- Okay, okay.
- Are you ready?

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.994
- Yes.
- Set, taste.

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:05.993
- Okay.
(cloches clink)

00:04:05.993 --> 00:04:06.826
(air horn sound)
(pensive music)

00:04:06.826 --> 00:04:08.792
Go, go, go, go, go.
(pensive music continues)

00:04:08.792 --> 00:04:09.793
- [Kelly] Shoot, uh.

00:04:09.793 --> 00:04:11.796
- [Kristen] You got 30
seconds, you gotta eat faster.

00:04:11.796 --> 00:04:12.646
- Wait, I can't.

00:04:12.646 --> 00:04:13.862
